WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.173
Allow 4 minutes.

00:00:01.413 --> 00:00:06.363
Bloom’s original cognitive taxonomy was published in 1956.

00:00:06.603 --> 00:00:16.373
This sample uses the 2001 revision associated with Anderson and Krathwohl: Remember, Understand, Apply, Analyze, Evaluate, and Create.

00:00:16.613 --> 00:00:21.840
The revision uses action-oriented category names and places Create after Evaluate.

00:00:22.080 --> 00:00:25.408
Do not silently mix these labels with the original list.

00:00:25.648 --> 00:00:30.619
University of Illinois Chicago and Iowa State provide background in Sources.

00:00:31.309 --> 00:00:41.843
A compact guide: Remember retrieves information; Understand makes meaning; Apply uses a procedure; Analyze examines parts and relationships; Evaluate

00:00:41.843 --> 00:00:46.967
judges against criteria; Create develops a coherent new product or plan.

00:00:47.207 --> 00:00:53.607
The revised framework also distinguishes factual, conceptual, procedural, and metacognitive knowledge.

00:00:53.847 --> 00:00:58.071
A task involves both what knowledge is used and what a learner does with it.

00:00:58.761 --> 00:01:08.439
Worked example: recalling the definition of an urgent ticket is Remember; explaining the distinction between urgent and routine is Understand; using a

00:01:08.439 --> 00:01:10.452
triage rule on a case is Apply.

00:01:10.692 --> 00:01:15.023
These are different tasks, even if every screen contains the word “priority.”

00:01:15.713 --> 00:01:18.059
The taxonomy is a classification aid.

00:01:18.299 --> 00:01:22.609
Choosing the highest-sounding label does not automatically improve training.

00:01:22.849 --> 00:01:27.563
In this sample, use the category that best describes the actual performance you need.

00:01:27.803 --> 00:01:31.110
A routine procedure can appropriately require Apply.

00:01:31.800 --> 00:01:32.888
Now it's your turn.

00:01:33.128 --> 00:01:39.144
A stakeholder asks you to label a routine record-entry task “Create” because it sounds more advanced.

00:01:39.384 --> 00:01:40.365
What should you do?

00:01:40.605 --> 00:01:43.720
Pause the video and make your choice in the activity below.

